Sends push notifications about system events to Telegram, Pushover,
ntfy, Gotify, Discord, Slack, Matrix, email, webhooks and the many other
services supported by Apprise. Channels are built from a service picker,
or from an Apprise URL you enter yourself, and each channel chooses which
events it receives.

Events: configuration changes (who changed what), logins and lockouts,
gateway down and recovery (with outage duration), VPN peers connecting
and disconnecting, new devices on the network, intrusion detection
alerts, Monit checks failing and recovering, firmware updates,
certificates nearing expiry, System Status notices, CARP state changes
and firewall startup.

Notifications that cannot be delivered, for example while the only WAN
is down, are retried with a backoff for up to 24 hours.

WWW: https://github.com/caronc/apprise
